1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:02,506
Islamabad, Pakistan.

2
00:00:02,506 --> 00:00:08,390
Through a back-channel, Iran and the United States sat down together.

3
00:00:08,390 --> 00:00:14,446
A draft 72-hour conditional pause arrived — Israel was not in the room.

4
00:00:14,446 --> 00:00:22,377
When Iran's delegate said Fordow was not on the agenda, the silence in the room grew heavier.

5
00:00:24,577 --> 00:00:29,470
Dr. Leila Shirazi confirmed the Fordow signal for the third time.

6
00:00:29,470 --> 00:00:36,547
Five days after the strike, a facility rated “fully neutralized” was pulsing again, regularly.

7
00:00:36,547 --> 00:00:43,699
Eighty meters underground, after two bunker-buster hits — something was still alive down there.

8
00:00:45,899 --> 00:00:53,378
The IAEA director-general raised the possibility that part of Fordow's structure had survived.

9
00:00:53,378 --> 00:01:06,904
Hours later, the Israeli PM's office issued a statement: “Israel retains the right to continue unilateral operations until Iran's nuclear capability is fully eliminated.”

10
00:01:06,904 --> 00:01:10,167
The 72-hour pause had no seat for Israel.

11
00:01:12,367 --> 00:01:19,165
Under a sky finally thinning of smoke, hundreds of thousands filled the square.

12
00:01:19,165 --> 00:01:25,533
Women without hijabs, old men with faded flags, parents carrying children.

13
00:01:25,533 --> 00:01:30,266
A Nowruz song rose three days before spring's new year.

14
00:01:30,266 --> 00:01:35,171
The IRGC held back — one Basij member set down his baton.

15
00:01:37,371 --> 00:01:45,745
The U.S. Navy's mine countermeasures force declared the northern shipping lane of the Strait of Hormuz clear.

16
00:01:45,745 --> 00:01:50,968
Limited tanker traffic resumed; oil eased slightly to $138 a barrel.

17
00:01:50,968 --> 00:01:58,113
The throat through which a fifth of the world's oil passes drew its first breath in six days.

18
00:02:00,313 --> 00:02:02,815
The air conditioning was broken.

19
00:02:02,815 --> 00:02:05,082
Twelve people sweated anyway.

20
00:02:05,082 --> 00:02:16,810
The U.S. deputy assistant secretary sat across from Iran's IRGC political liaison, with a Pakistani mediator between them who officially wasn't there.

21
00:02:16,810 --> 00:02:20,250
“Seventy-two hours,” the American side said.

22
00:02:20,250 --> 00:02:27,443
“In exchange: no new mines in Hormuz, no new ballistic launches, and IAEA access to Fordow.”

23
00:02:27,443 --> 00:02:31,430
The Iranian liaison said nothing for a long moment.

24
00:02:31,430 --> 00:02:35,418
“Fordow,” he finally said, “is not on this agenda.”

25
00:02:35,418 --> 00:02:42,532
“There's a signal coming out of Fordow,” the American side answered — quietly, but clearly.

26
00:02:42,532 --> 00:02:47,849
“Without that, there's nothing to discuss beyond seventy-two hours.”

27
00:02:47,849 --> 00:02:56,215
Wars begin with gunfire, but their real weight is often decided in rooms where no one says anything at all.

28
00:02:58,415 --> 00:03:02,147
Dr. Leila Shirazi checked the signal three times.

29
00:03:02,147 --> 00:03:06,184
First she thought it was an error, then interference.

30
00:03:06,184 --> 00:03:10,145
By the third check, she couldn't deny it any longer.

31
00:03:10,145 --> 00:03:17,077
Five days after two bunker-busters hit Fordow, the assessment had read “fully neutralized.”

32
00:03:17,077 --> 00:03:24,694
But the signal held a regular rhythm inside its irregularity — a truly dead system couldn't do that.

33
00:03:24,694 --> 00:03:26,903
She began writing the report.

34
00:03:26,903 --> 00:03:41,985
The last transmission from a source codenamed ZARRIN, routed through the Islamabad channel, had arrived with seven coordinates for a surviving sublevel and one line: “This is the last transmission.”

35
00:03:41,985 --> 00:03:44,727
The source's safety was in question.

36
00:03:44,727 --> 00:03:51,735
Seven months ago she'd written that only a kinetic intervention could change the trajectory.

37
00:03:51,735 --> 00:03:54,020
They'd made that intervention.

38
00:03:54,020 --> 00:03:58,590
If it hadn't been enough — what came next, she didn't write.

39
00:03:58,590 --> 00:04:00,038
Someone else would.

40
00:04:02,238 --> 00:04:10,059
Israel's prime minister received Washington's 72-hour proposal as a notification, not a consultation.

41
00:04:10,059 --> 00:04:18,422
He knew the difference well — and this notification meant Israel had been left out of the Islamabad channel.

42
00:04:18,422 --> 00:04:22,681
“Fordow is alive,” he told his chief of staff. “It is.”

43
00:04:22,681 --> 00:04:25,314
“Then our mission isn't finished.”

44
00:04:25,314 --> 00:04:26,321
That was all.

45
00:04:26,321 --> 00:04:39,872
The short sentence became an official statement within hours: “Israel retains the right to continue unilateral operations until Iran's nuclear capability is fully eliminated.”

46
00:04:39,872 --> 00:04:42,273
The world read it as a warning.

47
00:04:42,273 --> 00:04:47,926
It wasn't a warning — it was the announcement of a decision already made.

48
00:04:50,126 --> 00:04:56,300
Captain Marcus Webb was alone on the bridge when the mine-clearance report came in.

49
00:04:56,300 --> 00:05:04,781
One of the narrowest throats on earth, carrying a fifth of the world's oil, was opening again after six days shut.

50
00:05:04,781 --> 00:05:10,956
Sarah Callahan came up without her camera — for the first time since the war began.

51
00:05:10,956 --> 00:05:13,188
“The strait's open,” she said.

52
00:05:13,188 --> 00:05:14,601
“Limited,” he said.

53
00:05:14,601 --> 00:05:16,163
“Northern lane only.”

54
00:05:16,163 --> 00:05:17,726
“Still open, though.”

55
00:05:17,726 --> 00:05:19,734
He nodded without speaking.

56
00:05:19,734 --> 00:05:23,603
On the horizon, the silhouette of a tanker appeared.

57
00:05:23,603 --> 00:05:26,058
“I heard about Fordow,” she said.

58
00:05:26,058 --> 00:05:28,959
“It's not over, is it.” “Probably not.”

59
00:05:28,959 --> 00:05:33,943
He knew that the strait opening today didn't mean the war was over.

60
00:05:33,943 --> 00:05:37,068
Not while Fordow's signal was still alive.

61
00:05:39,268 --> 00:05:44,808
Captain Kim Junho sat with the phone in his hand for twenty minutes.

62
00:05:44,808 --> 00:05:47,252
Nine times he'd tried to call.

63
00:05:47,252 --> 00:05:51,244
Nine times he'd stopped just short of the button.

64
00:05:51,244 --> 00:06:00,694
Six days into the war, he hadn't called his parents once — afraid that his mother's voice would make all of it real.

65
00:06:00,694 --> 00:06:02,161
He finally dialed.

66
00:06:02,161 --> 00:06:06,804
She picked up on the second ring, past midnight in Seoul.

67
00:06:06,804 --> 00:06:08,352
She'd been waiting.

68
00:06:08,352 --> 00:06:09,004
“Junho.”

69
00:06:09,004 --> 00:06:11,122
Two syllables were enough.

70
00:06:11,122 --> 00:06:16,011
“I'm alive,” he said, his voice steadier than he'd expected.

71
00:06:16,011 --> 00:06:17,558
“I know,” she said.

72
00:06:17,558 --> 00:06:21,469
“We've been watching the news. Your father too.”

73
00:06:21,469 --> 00:06:27,498
A short silence, then her voice dropped to almost a whisper. “Sleep well.”

74
00:06:27,498 --> 00:06:33,934
She asked nothing else — not when he'd come home, not whether it was dangerous.

75
00:06:33,934 --> 00:06:39,637
Not asking was how she said: I already know everything, and I'll wait.

76
00:06:41,837 --> 00:06:48,990
Under a sky thinning of smoke, Soraya Tahir stood in the middle of Azadi Square and sang.

77
00:06:48,990 --> 00:06:59,037
Not a war song — an old Persian song for the end of winter, for flowers opening, one the revolution had never managed to ban.

78
00:06:59,037 --> 00:07:06,672
Women without hijabs, old men with faded flags, parents holding children joined in, one by one.

79
00:07:06,672 --> 00:07:10,771
The Basij came out onto Vali-e Asr Avenue that day.

80
00:07:10,771 --> 00:07:13,424
But they didn't move to crush it.

81
00:07:13,424 --> 00:07:18,407
One of them set his baton down on the pavement and sang along.

82
00:07:18,407 --> 00:07:21,782
Someone laid a spring flower on top of it.

83
00:07:21,782 --> 00:07:27,569
Two days later, that image would be shared more than any other on earth.

84
00:07:27,569 --> 00:07:29,820
The war had broken the city.

85
00:07:29,820 --> 00:07:34,160
But spring didn't stop — spring is older than the war.

86
00:07:36,360 --> 00:07:43,075
Professor Azad Moradi opened the last blank page of a notebook he'd bought in 1973.

87
00:07:43,075 --> 00:07:47,606
Yesterday's song from the square still rang in his ears.

88
00:07:47,606 --> 00:07:54,160
The smoke outside was thinner than yesterday's — the effect of the 72-hour pause.

89
00:07:54,160 --> 00:08:03,949
Whether that meant peace or simply a held breath, fifty-three years of teaching philosophy hadn't taught him how to know.

90
00:08:03,949 --> 00:08:15,600
He picked up his pen and wrote: “Fifty-three years ago, on this notebook's first page, I wrote — truth is uncomfortable, but a lie hurts longer.

91
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:21,102
Today, on the last page, I write this: freedom is uncomfortable too.

92
00:08:21,102 --> 00:08:23,448
But repression hurts longer.”

93
00:08:23,448 --> 00:08:25,309
He closed the notebook.

94
00:08:25,309 --> 00:08:28,788
From the courtyard, the singing rose again.

95
00:08:30,988 --> 00:08:33,384
Fordow's signal changed again.

96
00:08:33,384 --> 00:08:45,363
Its strength was rising — a last surge as residual power died, a restart by Iranian technicians underground, or the third possibility she feared most.

97
00:08:45,363 --> 00:08:48,558
There was no way to know which, not yet.

98
00:08:48,558 --> 00:08:58,381
IAEA access needed Iran's permission; Iran's permission needed progress in the talks; progress needed Israel to stand down.

99
00:08:58,381 --> 00:09:04,051
She knew, in numbers, how uncertain each link in that chain really was.

100
00:09:04,051 --> 00:09:06,048
She wrote another report.

101
00:09:06,048 --> 00:09:15,951
The final line was different from the one she'd written seven months earlier: “Kinetic intervention alone is not sufficient.

102
00:09:15,951 --> 00:09:18,187
The next step is diplomatic.

103
00:09:18,187 --> 00:09:23,059
Without it, Fordow's signal cannot be stopped.” She filed it.

104
00:09:23,059 --> 00:09:26,333
Ending a war is harder than starting one.

105
00:09:26,333 --> 00:09:31,604
Bombs bring down buildings — but a signal doesn't stop for a bomb.

106
00:09:31,604 --> 00:09:33,122
— End of Episode 3.

107
00:09:33,122 --> 00:09:35,118
Continued in Episode 4. —

